# Rootlake

> Rootlake LLC measures how mobile networks perform in the real world, and where. The data
> is collected first-party through Rootlake's own SDK, integrated by mobile app developers,
> and licensed to companies that build analytics and intelligence products on top of it.
> Rootlake is a data provider, not an advertising company.

## What Rootlake provides

Cellular network performance measurements — how a network is behaving on a device at a
given moment — together with location context for devices whose users have granted location
permission, and basic technical attributes such as device type and connection details.

Partners are typically location intelligence platforms, mobility and market analytics firms,
data platforms that build their own products on the feed, and telecom and infrastructure
companies working on coverage and benchmarking.

## How it is collected

App developers integrate the Rootlake SDK into their mobile applications. Measurements are
taken on the device only after the end user has given consent through the app's consent
management platform and granted the relevant permissions. Nothing is purchased from
advertising exchanges or third-party brokers, and location is never inferred from IP
addresses.

## Coverage

Markets across Europe, Latin America and Asia. The panel grows as new publishers integrate
the SDK, so coverage by country changes over time. Current breakdowns are shared with
prospective partners on request.

## Privacy position

- Consent is the lawful basis for everything collected, captured before any measurement is taken.
- Rootlake does not collect names, email addresses, phone numbers, message content or browsing history. Identifiers in the data are pseudonymous.
- Rootlake operates under the GDPR, the UK GDPR and the Swiss FADP, with appropriate transfer mechanisms and appointed representatives in the EU and the UK.
- Rootlake does not serve advertising and does not profile people for ad targeting.
- Licenses prohibit identifying or tracking individuals, inferring sensitive characteristics, and any use for government surveillance or law-enforcement targeting.
- End users can opt out at https://rootlake.io/opt-out or via privacy@rootlake.io.

## Delivery

Server-to-server, on a regular schedule, to a dedicated access-controlled location in a
format agreed with the partner. Technical specifications are shared under a mutual
non-disclosure agreement.

